From e93cc3581c25a4ecc03160c89f002aadac6b4ee8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sandro Guilliety <188060053+fokandzi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:09:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(auth): redact email-token links, atomic single-use
 tokens, wrap legacy SHA-256 passwords

Email tokens
- mail_log.body (and test-mode console output) stored the raw ?token= of every
  verify/reset link; a verify link signs its holder in. Bodies are now stored
  redacted; raw links only on a dev machine with PAWLS_DEV_MAIL_LINKS=1
- consume is one conditional UPDATE (matching hash + kind + unused + unexpired)
- a new reset link expires older unused ones; consuming expires siblings
- purgeExpiredEmailTokens() + scripts/security/purge-expired-email-tokens.ts
- migration 011: redact stored links, expire every live token, cleanup index

Legacy passwords
- sha256-scrypt$ format = scrypt(sha256hex(pw)); wraps a bare digest without
  the password (scripts/security/wrap-legacy-password-hashes.ts, dry-run first)
- login re-hashes legacy/wrapped/weak-param rows (compare-and-swap)

Login: per-account limit across rotating IPs.
scripts/security/readonly-security-audit.ts: counts only, read-only txn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
